      <activity id="7b2cffd2-4b56-5072-9487-861bd079cc40" activityNameId="5634898d-d278-52c7-adb4-7dc5b8dd3537" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Use, computer, desktop, mix, home use</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Use, computer, desktop, mix, home use
The ratio 36/64 (CRT/LCD) is based on a survey carried out in Japan. Market information on selling volumes supports the trend towards more and more LCD monitors. The computer home use is calculated according to the share between active, standby and off modes taken from literature information.;
Synonyms: PC; 
UUID: 3a1ff55d-90a1-3ed5-87c2-1cb69002c9e0
Describes a mixed use of a desktop computer with the ratio 36% CRT monitor and 64% LCD monitor. Calculated per 1 hour of computer use at home. UCTE production mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage). 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of the desktop computer, which is described in another dataset.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature, survey and assumptions 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3a1ff55d-90a1-3ed5-87c2-1cb69002c9e0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
